    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into the September 1st slate with **Gunnar Henderson** serving as our clear focal point. With a score of 83.29, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a premium matchup against Hughes (xERA 4.72) and a significant dynamic platoon advantage, making him an elite start for both counting stats and power production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Kyle Tucker** (72.48) also project as high-leverage assets today; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is particularly boosted by favorable wind conditions and a soft matchup against Rodriguez, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a plug-and-play efficiency engine regardless of the venue. We are also closely tracking **Jackson Merrill** (61.13), whose profile is elevated today by an exploitable delivery speed from Lodolo, creating a rare window for a stolen base opportunity in a challenging lefty-on-lefty matchup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board involved balancing **Henry Bolte** (54.06) against the rest of the outfield. While **Henry Bolte** earns points for his leadoff spot, the looming presence of Gore\u2014an arm that suppresses production\u2014capped his upside, ultimately favoring the higher-floor profiles of **Drake Baldwin** (67.76) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14). The most notable sit is **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (49.45), who is relegated to the bench despite his reputation; he faces the toughest pitcher of the day in Williams (xERA 2.97), and his efficiency score plummeted under the weight of that difficult matchup. While we navigate the absences of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** to the IL, our current depth provided by **Tommy White** and **Luis Lara** will need to maximize their peripheral contributions to stay competitive in the 5x5 race. Managers should keep a close eye on the weather, as any late-breaking updates impacting the outfielders could necessitate a shift to our utility reserves like **Nasim Nunez** or **Heliot Ramos**.",
